  "findings": [
    "Required first-year units carry 60 EC. Leiden Law Practices lists tutoring and language test at zero credits and a parent activity in the zero-credit group. Introduction to Private Law II assumes the preceding Private Law I.",
    "Year two consists of 45 EC compulsory, 5 EC restricted technology and law and 10 EC notarial electives. Second-year administrative and EU law require the corresponding first-year modules. The two obligations modules require Private Law I. Property and Family Law require both first-year private law modules, and Company Law presupposes knowledge of obligations and property. The chosen first-listed technology and law module adds no admission requirement.",
    "The current public programme overview gives subject areas and an eleven-week independent thesis, but lacks revised third-year credits and entry rules. The prior official overview and archived 2025–2026 guide document the earlier curriculum, not the revised third year. Nominal 2027–2028 and 2028–2029 API requests return the current 2026–2027 product. The exact outgoing thesis module specifies 5 EC and an older progression rule, which cannot be carried over."
  ],
